// =====================================================================
// RS canvas textures -- drawable surfaces for in-world UI billboards.
// ZScript draws on these with the full Font/Screen API
// (TexMan.GetCanvas in RS_UI.zs), and the engine's billboard renderer
// displays them in the world as depth-sorted camera-facing quads
// (payload BB_TEXTURE). One canvas per concurrently-visible panel.
// =====================================================================

// The weapon card -- 2:3 portrait, drawn by RS_UIHandler.RenderOverlay.
canvastexture "RSCARDA" 256 384

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// In-world panel faces (RS_Panel / RS_DropTriptych). 320x640, 1:2
// portrait -- taller than RSCARDA because a panel you lean toward and
// read carries far more than one pinned to your face, and the drop
// comparison wants every row it can get.
//
// NINE, because a stacked triptych is three weapons x three blocks
// (core stats, affixes, identity). Tall mode uses the first three and
// leaves the rest unbound, which costs nothing: a canvas is only
// rendered when something dirties it.
//
// One canvas PER PANEL is the simple shape and the right one at this
// count. It does not scale indefinitely -- binding a canvas as a
// material re-dirties it, so every visible canvas costs an offscreen
// render-target switch per frame. If the live panel count ever grows
// past a few dozen, the answer is one atlas canvas with per-panel UV
// subrects, not ninety of these.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
canvastexture "RSPNL01" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL02" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL03" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL04" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL05" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL06" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL07" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL08" 320 640
canvastexture "RSPNL09" 320 640

// The drop marker beam. ONE canvas shared by every beam in the map --
// it is painted once, as a white vertical gradient, and each beam
// panel tints it per weapon tier through fillcolor + AddStencil. So a
// map full of drops costs one canvas, not one per drop.
// 32 wide is deliberate: the beam is thin in the world and stretching
// a narrow texture across it wastes nothing.
canvastexture "RSPNLBM" 32 256
